01:05:20.000 --> 01:05:24.000
From faithful to atheist and everywhere in between

01:05:24.000 --> 01:05:28.000
I've done a great deal of work over the past few years

01:05:28.000 --> 01:05:32.000
And while I had an opportunity to be baptized in my former church

01:05:32.000 --> 01:05:36.000
Perhaps because I needed more time to do more work

01:05:36.000 --> 01:05:40.000
I know beyond a shadow of a doubt that I'm fully committed to continue on this journey

01:05:40.000 --> 01:05:44.000
That I'll continue to fail, but continue to try

01:05:44.000 --> 01:05:48.000
That I want my life and works to reflect Christ perfectly through my human imperfection

01:05:48.000 --> 01:05:52.000
I want my identity to be cemented in Christ and Christian community before all else

01:05:52.000 --> 01:05:56.000
My baptism today is a sign of my heartfelt commitment to this

01:05:56.000 --> 01:06:00.000
As a gay woman, I carry significant hurt and judgment

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:04.000
And exclusion, I'm sorry, I carry significant hurt and damage

01:06:04.000 --> 01:06:08.000
From judgment and exclusion from Christians and church in general

01:06:08.000 --> 01:06:12.000
I also carry incredible hurt and trauma

01:06:12.000 --> 01:06:16.000
From LGBTQ Christians excluding me

01:06:16.000 --> 01:06:20.000
And acting anything but Christ-like toward me

01:06:20.000 --> 01:06:24.000
This is a uniquely horrific pain that I expected to carry to my grave

01:06:24.000 --> 01:06:28.000
Over the past year and a half, I've slowly come to realize

01:06:28.000 --> 01:06:32.000
That my faith and the people within it are a healing balm

01:06:32.000 --> 01:06:36.000
That I never could have imagined into existence for myself

01:06:36.000 --> 01:06:40.000
My baptism today, in this place, is also a sign of my commitment to this church

01:06:40.000 --> 01:06:44.000
And to each of you here with me tonight

01:06:44.000 --> 01:06:48.000
Thank you for celebrating and encouraging me

01:06:48.000 --> 01:06:52.000
